ly pretending like he's  hawkeye and we also see a kid jumping on  a trampoline with a small captain  america shield kinda like a one for  toddlers that you would just go to  target and pick up so as these kids are  playing avengers natasha comes around  the corner stops her bike gets off and  takes her helmet off she looks up and  the house that she grew up in as a child  for those few years with her so-called  family with yelena bulova molina  vostakov and alexis shostakov aka the  red guardian and we can see that it's a  rather emotional scene for her as she is  staring at the house reminiscing of her  past clearly very emotional some of the  kids that were playing avengers walk by  her the kid with the captain america  shield runs right by her however the  little girl who was playing like she was  black widow recognizes her she walks up  slowly behind her checking to see if it  really is her natasha smiles at her then  the little girl realizing that it's her  holds up her arm with her pretend black  widow bracelet and gives her a little  black widow bite natasha holds up her  arm and pretends to do the same back to  her and that's the scene now keep in  mind this is not an alternate post  credit scene this is an alternate ending  which i assume will be released when the  movie actually comes out on dvd and  blu-ray or wherever you want to buy it  i'm sure it's going to come out with the  film but this would have replaced the  scene with mason where she rides up on  her bike and she gets the quinjet and  that scene really has more connections  to infinity war because we know that  after she gets in the quinjet she goes  and breaks some of her fellow heroes out  of the raft so i can definitely see why  they went with that scene instead of  this scene it connects a lot more to the  events that were about to happen in  infinity war however although in the  mcu's timeline infinity war had not  taken place yet in real life it had and  i think a lot of people realize what  natasha would go on to do she would go  on to fight in infinity war and then  avengers in-game and then ultimately die  and since we ourselves and a good  majority of the people know that i think  this alternate ending is a little bit  more emotional and i think it kind of  ties you into natasha just a little bit  more you feel for her one last time and  i think it really just depends on what  you would want to feel at the end of the  movie would you want to feel a more  emotional connection to natasha a kind  of happy emotional scene right here  where we see that she's inspired little  girls and little boys as a hero and not  as a russian assassin or would you have  wanted what we actually got a setup for  what happens in avengers in-game for  what we actually knew was going to  happen and i actually think that they  probably could have done both they could  have shown this scene and then shown the  other scene with mason now clearly the  movie was super long and they needed to  cut some parts but i feel like if you  took a little bit out of this scene and  then took a little bit from the scene  with mason and the quinjet you probably  could have put them both together  because think about this and this is  actually why i prefer this scene over  the quinjet scene this would have been  the last time that we saw black widow  the last time ever seen natasha on  screen if you take away all of the  different multiversal aspects of it the  variant aspects of it yes perhaps we  could see a variant of her one day or  maybe not depending on the recent  reports which i'll talk about at the end  but if you put all of that aside this  would be the last time that we actually  get to see natasha in the mcu on screen  and for that sole reason is why i  actually prefer this deleted alternate  ending why because it actually shows  natasha in a very good light because the  black widow movie is all about her this  is her film it's about her tackling her  past it's about her coming face to face  with dracob again about her coming face  to face with antonia drakov's daughter  who they had been teasing us since the  very first avengers film the whole story  is that she was an assassin before she  killed a lot of people but ultimately  she turned good and did what she had to  do to go down the right path and in the  movie they actually kind of talk about  this yolina and natasha natasha says i  was trying to do something good be more  than just a trained killer and yelena  says you're fooling yourself we are  still both trained killers i'm not the  killer that little girls call their hero  this is a direct reference to that line  that yelena drops that exact  conversation where natasha is clearly  stating that she wants to be more than  what she had been she wants to be a hero  and what this scene does is actually  solidify the fact that she is indeed a  hero and she's a hero not only to us but  to the actual people inside the mcu she  made a real impact little girls and  little boys are pretending to be her  because they look up to her and that's  why i personally really like this scene  better than the one that we got not that  i didn't really like it i just would  have preferred this one i think it means  a lot more to the actual character  because we already knew that she was  gonna go break people out of the raft  and go start the events that happened  right before infinity war and then jump  into infinity war and end game but let  me know which one you would prefer in  the comments down below and like i  mentioned there has been some news about  the scarlett johansson lawsuit against  disney according to some reports online  disney has banned scarlett johansson  cameos in any further mcu movies not  like that would ultimately matter  because again we know she's dead but if  this is true this kind of eliminates any  possibility for her popping up as a  different variant of herself down the  road now a lot of people have asked me  about th